IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 4, Division 7 -- Title and transfers, public companies: transfer of shares and debentures, registration at the transferor's request, notice of refusal,
-- transfer by a personal representative, certification of prima facie title, duties as to certificates (ss 130 to 130AE); Division 7A (ss 130A to 130P) is repealed.
-- Layer 1, part agent sgj. Source file lines 10750-11034. The text is a rendering of the Act, not the official text.
-- HOW IT IS MODELLED: as in sgj-div7-private-transfers.l4. Taken as a fact from another part (PLAN.md section 4): `the company is a public company` (s 4(1) "public company").
-- The clock of the traces counts days after the event named in each rule.

§ `Section 130: transfer of shares and debentures in public companies`

DECLARE `s 130 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 130(1) register a transfer of shares or debentures without a proper instrument of transfer having been delivered to the company`

-- s 130(1): a public company must not register a transfer of shares or debentures unless a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered; this does not affect the power to register a person to whom the right has been transmitted by operation of law.
-- src:10754 | 130.—(1) Despite anything in its constitution, a public company
-- src:10755 | must not register a transfer of shares or debentures unless a proper
-- src:10756 | instrument of transfer has been delivered to the company, but this
-- src:10757 | subsection does not affect any power to register as a shareholder or
-- src:10758 | debenture holder any person to whom the right to any shares in or
-- src:10759 | debentures of the company has been transmitted by operation of law.
@ref s 130(1) (src:10754-10759)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right to the shares or debentures has been transmitted to the person by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(1) the public company is barred from registering the transfer of shares or debentures` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a public company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a public company must not register a transfer of shares or debentures" -- a scope limit with no "only"; the private company's rules are ss 126 and 127
    ELSE IF `the right to the shares or debentures has been transmitted to the person by operation of law`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this subsection does not affect any power to register as a shareholder or debenture holder any person to whom the right to any shares in or debentures of the company has been transmitted by operation of law"
         ELSE IF `a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered to the company`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not register a transfer of shares or debentures unless a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered to the company" -- the bar is closed with "unless"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 130(1) (src:10754-10759)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 130 act`
`s 130(1) a public company must not register a transfer of shares or debentures without a proper instrument of transfer` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 130(1) register a transfer of shares or debentures without a proper instrument of transfer having been delivered to the company`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company registered a transfer of shares or debentures without a proper instrument of transfer having been delivered to it"

-- s 130(2): where there has been a transfer of shares, a public company may lodge a notice with the Registrar.
-- A "may" gated by "where" on the company's own liberty to lodge: answered NOTHING by the S1b ruling (2026S1bC; item (b) of the periods ruling of 2026-11-05 would give JUST FALSE) and listed for a lawyer (fork F-j130-1, split site (ii)).
-- src:10763 | (2) Where there has been a transfer of shares, a public company
-- src:10764 | may lodge with the Registrar a notice of that transfer of shares in the
-- src:10765 | prescribed form.
@ref s 130(2) (src:10763-10765)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been a transfer of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(2) the public company may lodge with the Registrar a notice of the transfer of shares in the prescribed form` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a public company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a public company may lodge" -- a scope limit with no "only"; the private company's rule is s 126(2)
    ELSE IF `there has been a transfer of shares`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (a company's or person's liberty, no bar to relieve; S1b ruling 2026S1bC): "Where there has been a transfer of shares, a public company may lodge" -- a failed "where" gate on the company's own liberty to lodge (listed for a lawyer; the other reading is JUST FALSE, item (b) of the periods ruling of 2026-11-05)

-- s 130(3): the notice must state (a) every other transfer effected before the date of the notice, other than one previously notified; or (b) the prescribed information on the 50 largest members.
-- The text says "or" between (a) and (b): taken as written, so stating either suffices (fork F-j130-2; the other reading is "and").
-- src:10769 | (3) The notice must state —
-- src:10771 | (a) every other transfer of shares effected prior to the date of
-- src:10772 | the notice, other than a transfer that has been previously
-- src:10773 | notified to the Registrar; or
-- src:10778 | (b) the prescribed information in relation to the shares held by
-- src:10779 | each of the 50 members who hold the most number of
-- src:10780 | shares in the public company after the transfer.
@ref s 130(3) (src:10769-10780)
GIVEN `the notice is a notice of a transfer of shares lodged by a public company under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states every other transfer of shares effected prior to the date of the notice, other than a transfer that has been previously notified to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the prescribed information in relation to the shares held by each of the 50 members who hold the most number of shares in the public company after the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130(3) the notice states what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the notice is a notice of a transfer of shares lodged by a public company under subsection (2)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The notice must state" -- the notice of subsection (2); another notice is outside the text
    ELSE IF `the notice states every other transfer of shares effected prior to the date of the notice, other than a transfer that has been previously notified to the Registrar`
              OR `the notice states the prescribed information in relation to the shares held by each of the 50 members who hold the most number of shares in the public company after the transfer`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must state (a) every other transfer ...; or (b) the prescribed information ..." -- a duty: the provision's own question

§ `Section 130AA: registration of transfer at request of transferor by public companies`

DECLARE `s 130AA act` IS ONE OF
    `s 130AA(1) enter in the appropriate register the name of the transferee`
    `s 130AA(2) require by written notice the person having possession, custody or control to deliver or produce the share certificate or debenture and the instrument of transfer`
    `s 130AA(5) exhibit and advertise the list of share certificates or debentures called in and not brought in`

-- s 130AA(1): on the transferor's written request the company must enter the transferee's name in the appropriate register. No time is stated.
-- src:10787 | 130AA.—(1) On the request in writing of the transferor of any
-- src:10788 | share, debenture or other interest in a public company the company
-- src:10789 | must enter in the appropriate register the name of the transferee in the
-- src:10790 | same manner and subject to the same conditions as if the application
-- src:10791 | for the entry were made by the transferee.
@ref s 130AA(1) (src:10787-10791)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferor of the share, debenture or other interest has made the request in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AA(1) the public company must enter the name of the transferee in the appropriate register` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` AND `the transferor of the share, debenture or other interest has made the request in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the request in writing of the transferor ... the company must" -- the duty is limited by the written request; without it, or for another company, the text is silent (fork F-j130AA-1, as F-j128-1)

@ref s 130AA(1) (src:10787-10791)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 130AA act`
`s 130AA(1) a public company must enter the name of the transferee on the transferor's request` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 130AA(1) enter in the appropriate register the name of the transferee`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 130AA(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company did not enter the name of the transferee in the appropriate register on the written request of the transferor" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- s 130AA(2): the notice requiring delivery within a stated period of not less than 7 and not more than 28 days after the date of the notice.
-- src:10795 | (2) On the request in writing of the transferor of a share or
-- src:10796 | debenture the public company must by written notice require the
-- src:10797 | person having the possession, custody or control of the share
-- src:10798 | certificate or debenture and the instrument of transfer thereof or either
-- src:10799 | of them to deliver or produce it or them to the office of the company
-- src:10800 | within a stated period, being not less than 7 and not more than 28 days
-- src:10801 | after the date of the notice, to have the share certificate or debenture
-- src:10802 | cancelled or rectified and the transfer registered or otherwise dealt
-- src:10803 | with.
@ref s 130AA(2) (src:10795-10803)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferor of the share or debenture has made the request in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AA(2) the public company must by written notice require delivery or production of the documents` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` AND `the transferor of the share or debenture has made the request in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the request in writing of the transferor of a share or debenture the public company must" -- without the written request, or for another company, the text is silent

@ref s 130AA(2) (src:10795-10803)
GIVEN `the number of days after the date of the notice that the notice states` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AA(2) the period stated in the notice is a period the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the number of days after the date of the notice that the notice states` AT LEAST 7 AND `the number of days after the date of the notice that the notice states` AT MOST 28
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within a stated period, being not less than 7 and not more than 28 days after the date of the notice"

@ref s 130AA(2) (src:10795-10803)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 130AA act`
`s 130AA(2) a public company must require delivery or production of the documents by written notice` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 130AA(2) require by written notice the person having possession, custody or control to deliver or produce the share certificate or debenture and the instrument of transfer`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 130AA(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company did not require by written notice the person having possession, custody or control to deliver or produce the documents" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- s 130AA(3): if a person refuses or neglects to comply with the notice, the transferor may apply to a judge for a summons. A grant gated by "if": NOTHING (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-j130AA-2).
-- src:10807 | (3) If any person refuses or neglects to comply with a notice given
-- src:10808 | under subsection (2), the transferor may apply to a judge to issue a
-- src:10809 | summons for that person to appear before the Court and show cause
-- src:10810 | why the documents mentioned in the notice should not be delivered or
-- src:10811 | produced as required by the notice.
@ref s 130AA(3) (src:10807-10811)
GIVEN `the person has refused or neglected to comply with a notice given under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AA(3) the transferor may apply to a judge for a summons` MEANS
    IF `the person has refused or neglected to comply with a notice given under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If any person refuses or neglects to comply with a notice given under subsection (2), the transferor may apply to a judge" -- a grant whose "if" gate is unmet

-- s 130AA(4): upon appearance (or non-appearance after due service) the Court may order delivery. A "may" gated by "upon": item (b) of the periods ruling, "upon" counting as "where" under item (c) of the delegated-definitions ruling (fork F-j130AA-3, split site (ii)).
-- src:10815 | (4) Upon appearance of a person so summoned the Court may
-- src:10816 | examine the person upon oath and receive other evidence, or if the
-- src:10817 | person does not appear after being duly served with such summons,
-- src:10818 | the Court may receive evidence in the person’s absence and in either
-- src:10819 | case the Court may order the person to deliver such documents to the
-- src:10820 | company upon such terms or conditions as to the Court seem fit, and
-- src:10821 | the costs of the summons and proceedings thereon are in the
-- src:10822 | discretion of the Court.
@ref s 130AA(4) (src:10815-10822)
GIVEN `the person has been summoned under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has appeared` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has not appeared after being duly served with the summons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AA(4) the Court may order the person to deliver the documents to the company` MEANS
    IF `the person has been summoned under subsection (3)` AND (`the person has appeared` OR `the person has not appeared after being duly served with the summons`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, by item (b) of the periods ruling and item (c) of the delegated-definitions ruling, both of 2026-11-05): "Upon appearance of a person so summoned ... or if the person does not appear after being duly served ..., the Court may order the person to deliver such documents" -- a "may" gated by "upon" (listed for a lawyer)

-- s 130AA(5): the lists of share certificates or debentures called in and not brought in must be exhibited in the company's office and advertised. No time is stated.
-- src:10829 | (5) Lists of share certificates or debentures called in under this
-- src:10830 | section and not brought in must be exhibited in the office of the
-- src:10831 | company and must be advertised in such newspapers and at such
-- src:10832 | times as the company thinks fit.
@ref s 130AA(5) (src:10829-10832)
GIVEN `share certificates or debentures have been called in under section 130AA and have not been brought in` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AA(5) the company must exhibit the list in its office and advertise it` MEANS
    IF `share certificates or debentures have been called in under section 130AA and have not been brought in`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Lists of share certificates or debentures called in under this section and not brought in"

@ref s 130AA(5) (src:10829-10832)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 130AA act`
`s 130AA(5) the company must exhibit and advertise the list` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 130AA(5) exhibit and advertise the list of share certificates or debentures called in and not brought in`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 130AA(5) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not exhibit in its office and advertise the list of share certificates or debentures called in and not brought in" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

§ `Section 130AB: notice of refusal to register transfer by public companies`

DECLARE `s 130AB act` IS ONE OF
    `s 130AB(1) send to the transferor and to the transferee notice of the refusal to register a transfer`

-- s 130AB(1): within 30 days after the date on which the transfer was lodged with the company (the day of lodging is not counted: sg-periods P1).
-- src:10838 | 130AB.—(1) If a public company refuses to register a transfer of
-- src:10839 | any share, debenture or other interest in the company it must, within
-- src:10840 | 30 days after the date on which the transfer was lodged with it, send to
-- src:10841 | the transferor and to the transferee notice of the refusal.
@ref s 130AB(1) (src:10838-10841)
GIVEN `the day the transfer was lodged with the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 130AB(1) the last day for sending notice of the refusal` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the transfer was lodged with the company` 30 Days

@ref s 130AB(1) (src:10838-10841)
GIVEN `the day the transfer was lodged with the company` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice of the refusal was sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AB(1) the notice of the refusal was sent within 30 days` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice of the refusal was sent` AT MOST (`s 130AB(1) the last day for sending notice of the refusal` `the day the transfer was lodged with the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must, within 30 days after the date on which the transfer was lodged with it, send to the transferor and to the transferee notice of the refusal" -- a period the text fixes in its own words

@ref s 130AB(1) (src:10838-10841)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 130AB act`
`s 130AB(1) a public company that refuses to register a transfer must send notice of the refusal within 30 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 130AB(1) send to the transferor and to the transferee notice of the refusal to register a transfer`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company did not send to the transferor and to the transferee notice of the refusal within 30 days after the date on which the transfer was lodged"

-- s 130AB(2): the company must not refuse registration by virtue of a discretion in the constitution unless it has served a written notice of the facts within 30 days beginning with the day the application was made (sg-periods P10).
-- src:10845 | (2) Where an application is made to a public company for a person
-- src:10846 | to be registered as a member in respect of shares which have been
-- src:10847 | transferred or transmitted to the person by act of parties or operation
-- src:10848 | of law, the company must not refuse registration by virtue of any
-- src:10849 | discretion in that behalf conferred by its constitution unless it has
-- src:10850 | served on the applicant, within 30 days beginning with the day on
-- src:10851 | which the application was made, a written notice stating the facts
-- src:10852 | which are considered to justify refusal in the exercise of that
-- src:10853 | discretion.
@ref s 130AB(2) (src:10845-10853)
GIVEN `the day the application was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 130AB(2) the last day for serving the written notice` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the day the application was made` 30 Days

@ref s 130AB(2) (src:10845-10853)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is for a person to be registered as a member in respect of shares that have been transferred or transmitted to the person by act of parties or operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the application was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal was served on the applicant` IS A DATE
      `a written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal in the exercise of that discretion has been served on the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AB(2) the public company is barred from refusing registration by virtue of a discretion in the constitution` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company`) OR (NOT `the application is for a person to be registered as a member in respect of shares that have been transferred or transmitted to the person by act of parties or operation of law`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an application is made to a public company for a person to be registered as a member in respect of shares which have been transferred or transmitted to the person by act of parties or operation of law" -- a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE IF `a written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal in the exercise of that discretion has been served on the applicant`
              AND (`the day the written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal was served on the applicant` AT MOST (`s 130AB(2) the last day for serving the written notice` `the day the application was made`))
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not refuse registration ... unless it has served on the applicant, within 30 days beginning with the day on which the application was made, a written notice stating the facts" -- the bar is closed with "unless"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 130AB(2) as a regulative rule: the prohibition is on refusing without the notice. The act carries whether the notice was served in time; refusing with no timely notice is BREACH.
DECLARE `s 130AB(2) refusal` IS ONE OF
    `s 130AB(2) refusal by virtue of a discretion` HAS `the written notice was served on the applicant within 30 days beginning with the day the application was made` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 130AB(2) (src:10845-10853)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 130AB(2) refusal`
`s 130AB(2) a public company must not refuse registration by virtue of a discretion without a timely written notice` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 130AB(2) refusal by virtue of a discretion` served PROVIDED NOT served
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company refused registration by virtue of a discretion in the constitution without having served a written notice stating the facts within 30 days beginning with the day of the application"

-- s 130AB(3): the offence of default.
-- src:10857 | (3) If default is made in complying with this section, the public
-- src:10858 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall
-- src:10859 | each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a
-- src:10860 | fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 130AB(3) (src:10857-10860)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 130AB` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AB(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 130AB` AND (`the person is the public company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section, the public company and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet (split site (i), fork line F-j130AB-1)

@ref s 130AB(3) (src:10857-10860)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 130AB` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 130AB(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 130AB(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 130AB` `the person is the public company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    --                          fine, months, both, default penalty
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Section 130AC: transfer by personal representative`

DECLARE `s 130AC act` IS ONE OF
    `s 130AC(2) accept the document as sufficient evidence of the grant`

-- s 130AC(1): a transfer by a deceased person's personal representative is as valid as if the representative had been a member when the instrument was executed.
-- src:10866 | 130AC.—(1) A transfer of the share, debenture or other interest of
-- src:10867 | a deceased person made by the deceased person’s personal
-- src:10868 | representative is, although the personal representative is not
-- src:10869 | himself or herself a member of the company, as valid as if he or
-- src:10870 | she had been such a member at the time of the execution of the
-- src:10871 | instrument of transfer.
@ref s 130AC(1) (src:10866-10871)
GIVEN `the transfer is of the share, debenture or other interest of a deceased person and is made by the deceased person's personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AC(1) the transfer is as valid as if the personal representative had been a member of the company at the time of the execution of the instrument of transfer` MEANS
    IF `the transfer is of the share, debenture or other interest of a deceased person and is made by the deceased person's personal representative`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A transfer of the share, debenture or other interest of a deceased person made by the deceased person's personal representative" -- a deeming limited to that transfer

-- s 130AC(2): a document that is by law sufficient evidence of probate or letters of administration must be accepted by the company, despite its constitution, as sufficient evidence of the grant. No time is stated.
-- src:10875 | (2) The production to a company of any document which is by law
-- src:10876 | sufficient evidence of probate of the will, or letters of administration
-- src:10881 | of the estate, of a deceased person having been granted to some
-- src:10882 | person must be accepted by the company, despite anything in its
-- src:10883 | constitution, as sufficient evidence of the grant.
@ref s 130AC(2) (src:10875-10883)
GIVEN `the document has been produced to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is by law sufficient evidence of probate of the will, or letters of administration of the estate, of a deceased person having been granted to some person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AC(2) the company must accept the document as sufficient evidence of the grant` MEANS
    IF `the document has been produced to the company` AND `the document is by law sufficient evidence of probate of the will, or letters of administration of the estate, of a deceased person having been granted to some person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The production to a company of any document which is by law sufficient evidence of probate of the will, or letters of administration of the estate, of a deceased person" -- the duty is limited to such a document

@ref s 130AC(2) (src:10875-10883)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 130AC act`
`s 130AC(2) a company must accept the document as sufficient evidence of the grant` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 130AC(2) accept the document as sufficient evidence of the grant`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 130AC(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not accept the document produced to it as sufficient evidence of the grant of probate or letters of administration" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: maintenance; see notes]

-- s 130AC(3): "instrument of transfer" includes a written application for transmission to a personal representative. An "includes" list is not closed.
-- src:10887 | (3) In this section, “instrument of transfer” includes a written
-- src:10888 | application for transmission of a share, debenture or other interest to a
-- src:10889 | personal representative.
@ref s 130AC(3) (src:10887-10889)
GIVEN `the document is a written application for transmission of a share, debenture or other interest to a personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AC(3) "instrument of transfer" the document is an instrument of transfer for the purposes of section 130AC` MEANS
    IF `the document is a written application for transmission of a share, debenture or other interest to a personal representative`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "In this section, 'instrument of transfer' includes a written application for transmission of a share, debenture or other interest to a personal representative" -- an "includes" definition does not close the list

§ `Section 130AD: certification of prima facie title`

-- s 130AD(1): the certification of an instrument of transfer is taken as a representation, to a person acting on its faith, that documents showing a prima facie title in the transferor have been produced to the company, but not as a representation that the transferor has any title.
-- src:10898 | 130AD.—(1) The certification by a company of any instrument of
-- src:10899 | transfer of shares, debentures or other interests in the company is to
-- src:10900 | be taken as a representation by the company to any person acting on
-- src:10901 | the faith of the certification that there have been produced to the
-- src:10902 | company such documents as on the face of them show a prima facie
-- src:10903 | title to the shares, debentures or other interests in the transferor
-- src:10904 | named in the instrument of transfer but not as a representation that the
-- src:10905 | transferor has any title to the shares, debentures or other interests.
@ref s 130AD(1) (src:10898-10905)
GIVEN `the company has certified an instrument of transfer of shares, debentures or other interests in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is acting on the faith of the certification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AD(1) the certification is taken as a representation that documents showing a prima facie title in the transferor have been produced to the company` MEANS
    IF `the company has certified an instrument of transfer of shares, debentures or other interests in the company` AND `the person is acting on the faith of the certification`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The certification by a company of any instrument of transfer ... is to be taken as a representation by the company to any person acting on the faith of the certification" -- a deeming limited to a person acting on the faith of it

@ref s 130AD(1) (src:10898-10905)
GIVEN `the company has certified an instrument of transfer of shares, debentures or other interests in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AD(1) the certification is taken as a representation that the transferor has any title` MEANS
    IF `the company has certified an instrument of transfer of shares, debentures or other interests in the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but not as a representation that the transferor has any title to the shares, debentures or other interests" -- a flat negative
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the negative is stated of the certification of an instrument of transfer

-- s 130AD(2): where a person acts on the faith of a false certification made negligently, the company is under the same liability as if it had been made fraudulently.
-- A liability whose "where" is unmet: the periods ruling's item (b) says JUST FALSE, as at s 83(1) (fork F-j130AD-1).
-- src:10909 | (2) Where any person acts on the faith of a false certification by a
-- src:10910 | company made negligently, the company is under the same liability to
-- src:10911 | the person as if the certification had been made fraudulently.
@ref s 130AD(2) (src:10909-10911)
GIVEN `the person acts on the faith of a false certification by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certification was made negligently` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AD(2) the company is under the same liability to the person as if the certification had been made fraudulently` MEANS
    IF `the person acts on the faith of a false certification by the company` AND `the certification was made negligently`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, by item (b) of the periods ruling of 2026-11-05): "Where any person acts on the faith of a false certification by a company made negligently, the company is under the same liability" -- a liability whose "where" is unmet

-- s 130AD(3), (4): a certification expressed to be limited to 42 days or any longer period from the date of certification.
-- The period ends on the day the certification's days after its date run out, plus any extension the company gave; a transfer on a later day is "after the expiration" (sg-periods P1).
-- src:10915 | (3) Where any certification by a private company is expressed to be
-- src:10916 | limited to 42 days or any longer period from the date of certification,
-- src:10917 | the company and its officers shall not, in the absence of fraud, be
-- src:10918 | liable —
-- src:10920 | (a) in respect of any transfer of shares after the expiration of
-- src:10921 | the period so limited or any extension thereof given by the
-- src:10922 | company if the instrument of transfer has not been sent to
-- src:10923 | or received by the company under section 126(1) within
-- src:10924 | that period; or
-- src:10926 | (b) in respect of the registration of any transfer of debentures
-- src:10927 | or other interests comprised in the certification after the
-- src:10928 | expiration of the period so limited or any extension thereof
-- src:10929 | given by the company if the instrument of transfer has not
-- src:10930 | within that period been lodged with the company for
-- src:10931 | registration.
@ref s 130AD(3) (src:10915-10931)
GIVEN `the day of the certification` IS A DATE
      `the number of days to which the certification is limited` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days by which the company has extended the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 130AD(3) the last day of the period so limited or any extension of it` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the certification` (`the number of days to which the certification is limited` PLUS `the number of days by which the company has extended the period`) Days

@ref s 130AD(3) (src:10915-10931)
GIVEN `the certification was made by a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days to which the certification is limited` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the certification` IS A DATE
      `the number of days by which the company has extended the period` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the transfer` IS A DATE
      `the instrument of transfer has been sent to or received by the company under section 126(1) within that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AD(3)(a) the company and its officers are liable in respect of the transfer of shares` MEANS
    IF `the certification was made by a private company`
       AND `the number of days to which the certification is limited` AT LEAST 42
       AND (NOT `there has been fraud`)
       AND (NOT (`the day of the transfer` AT MOST (`s 130AD(3) the last day of the period so limited or any extension of it` `the day of the certification` `the number of days to which the certification is limited` `the number of days by which the company has extended the period`)))
       AND (NOT `the instrument of transfer has been sent to or received by the company under section 126(1) within that period`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company and its officers shall not, in the absence of fraud, be liable in respect of any transfer of shares after the expiration of the period so limited or any extension thereof given by the company if the instrument of transfer has not been sent to or received by the company under section 126(1) within that period" -- a flat negative
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where any certification by a private company is expressed to be limited to 42 days or any longer period", "in the absence of fraud", "after the expiration", "if the instrument of transfer has not been sent" -- outside them the text does not say the company is liable

@ref s 130AD(3) (src:10915-10931)
GIVEN `the certification was made by a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days to which the certification is limited` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the certification` IS A DATE
      `the number of days by which the company has extended the period` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the registration of the transfer` IS A DATE
      `the instrument of transfer has within that period been lodged with the company for registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AD(3)(b) the company and its officers are liable in respect of the registration of the transfer of debentures or other interests` MEANS
    IF `the certification was made by a private company`
       AND `the number of days to which the certification is limited` AT LEAST 42
       AND (NOT `there has been fraud`)
       AND (NOT (`the day of the registration of the transfer` AT MOST (`s 130AD(3) the last day of the period so limited or any extension of it` `the day of the certification` `the number of days to which the certification is limited` `the number of days by which the company has extended the period`)))
       AND (NOT `the instrument of transfer has within that period been lodged with the company for registration`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company and its officers shall not, in the absence of fraud, be liable in respect of the registration of any transfer of debentures or other interests comprised in the certification after the expiration of the period so limited or any extension thereof given by the company if the instrument of transfer has not within that period been lodged with the company for registration" -- a flat negative
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where any certification by a private company is expressed to be limited to 42 days or any longer period", "in the absence of fraud", "after the expiration", "if the instrument of transfer has not ... been lodged" -- outside them the text does not say the company is liable

-- src:10935 | (4) Where any certification by a public company is expressed to be
-- src:10936 | limited to 42 days or any longer period from the date of certification,
-- src:10937 | the company and its officers shall not, in the absence of fraud, be
-- src:10938 | liable in respect of the registration of any transfer of shares,
-- src:10939 | debentures or other interests comprised in the certification after the
