      `the day of the registration of the transfer` IS A DATE
      `the instrument of transfer has within that period been lodged with the company for registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AD(4) the company and its officers are liable in respect of the registration of the transfer of shares, debentures or other interests` MEANS
    IF `the certification was made by a public company`
       AND `the number of days to which the certification is limited` AT LEAST 42
       AND (NOT `there has been fraud`)
       AND (NOT (`the day of the registration of the transfer` AT MOST (`s 130AD(3) the last day of the period so limited or any extension of it` `the day of the certification` `the number of days to which the certification is limited` `the number of days by which the company has extended the period`)))
       AND (NOT `the instrument of transfer has within that period been lodged with the company for registration`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company and its officers shall not, in the absence of fraud, be liable in respect of the registration of any transfer of shares, debentures or other interests comprised in the certification after the expiration of the period so limited or any extension thereof given by the company if the instrument of transfer has not within that period been lodged with the company for registration" -- a flat negative
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where any certification by a public company is expressed to be limited to 42 days or any longer period", "in the absence of fraud", "after the expiration", "if the instrument of transfer has not within that period been lodged" -- outside them the text does not say the company is liable

-- s 130AD(5)(a): an instrument of transfer is treated as certificated if it bears the words "certificate lodged" or words to the like effect.
-- A deeming "if" gives a sufficient condition and does not say "only": NOTHING when it is unmet (fork F-j130AD-2, as F-j93-1).
-- src:10950 | (5) For the purposes of this section —
-- src:10952 | (a) an instrument of transfer is to be treated as certificated if it
-- src:10953 | bears the words “certificate lodged” or words to the like
-- src:10954 | effect;
@ref s 130AD(5)(a) (src:10950-10954)
GIVEN `the instrument of transfer bears the words "certificate lodged" or words to the like effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AD(5)(a) the instrument of transfer is treated as certificated` MEANS
    IF `the instrument of transfer bears the words "certificate lodged" or words to the like effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an instrument of transfer is to be treated as certificated if it bears the words" -- a deeming "if" with no "only"

-- s 130AD(5)(b): the certification is treated as made by the company if (i) the person issuing the instrument is apparently authorised to issue certificated instruments on the company's behalf; and
-- (ii) the certification is signed by a person apparently authorised to certificate transfers on the company's behalf or by any officer of the company or of a corporation so apparently authorised.
-- src:10956 | (b) the certification of an instrument of transfer is to be treated
-- src:10957 | as made by a company if —
-- src:10959 | (i) the person issuing the instrument is a person
-- src:10960 | apparently authorised to issue certificated
-- src:10961 | instruments of transfer on the company’s behalf; and
-- src:10963 | (ii) the certification is signed by a person apparently
-- src:10964 | authorised to certificate transfers on the company’s
-- src:10965 | behalf or by any officer either of the company or of a
-- src:10966 | corporation so apparently authorised; and
@ref s 130AD(5)(b) (src:10956-10966)
GIVEN `the person issuing the instrument is a person apparently authorised to issue certificated instruments of transfer on the company's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certification is signed by a person apparently authorised to certificate transfers on the company's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certification is signed by an officer either of the company or of a corporation so apparently authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AD(5)(b) the certification of the instrument of transfer is treated as made by the company` MEANS
    IF `the person issuing the instrument is a person apparently authorised to issue certificated instruments of transfer on the company's behalf`
       AND (`the certification is signed by a person apparently authorised to certificate transfers on the company's behalf` OR `the certification is signed by an officer either of the company or of a corporation so apparently authorised`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is to be treated as made by a company if" -- a deeming "if" with no "only"

-- s 130AD(5)(c): in the text this paragraph is lettered (c) although it sits inside the run of (b) (finding in NOTES.md).
-- A certification that purports to be authenticated by a signature or initials is deemed signed by the person unless it is shown that neither the person nor another apparently authorised person placed them.
-- src:10968 | (c) a certification that purports to be authenticated by a
-- src:10969 | person’s signature or initials (whether handwritten or not)
-- src:10970 | is deemed to be signed by the person unless it is shown that
-- src:10971 | the signature or initials were not placed there by the person
-- src:10972 | and were not placed there by any other person apparently
-- src:10973 | authorised to use the signature or initials for the purpose of
-- src:10974 | certificating transfers on the company’s behalf.
@ref s 130AD(5)(c) (src:10968-10974)
GIVEN `the certification purports to be authenticated by a person's signature or initials` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is shown that the signature or initials were not placed there by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is shown that the signature or initials were not placed there by any other person apparently authorised to use them for the purpose of certificating transfers on the company's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AD(5)(c) the certification is deemed to be signed by the person` MEANS
    IF NOT `the certification purports to be authenticated by a person's signature or initials`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a certification that purports to be authenticated by a person's signature or initials" -- the deeming is limited to such a certification
    ELSE IF `it is shown that the signature or initials were not placed there by the person` AND `it is shown that the signature or initials were not placed there by any other person apparently authorised to use them for the purpose of certificating transfers on the company's behalf`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to be signed by the person unless it is shown that the signature or initials were not placed there by the person and were not placed there by any other person apparently authorised" -- the deeming is closed with "unless"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 130AE: duties of company with respect to issue of certificates and default in issue of certificates`

DECLARE `s 130AE act` IS ONE OF
    `s 130AE(1) complete and have ready for delivery all the appropriate certificates and debentures in connection with the allotment`
    `s 130AE(1) complete and have ready for delivery all the appropriate certificates and debentures in connection with the transfer`
    `s 130AE(2)(a) complete and have ready for delivery all the appropriate certificates and debentures in connection with the allotment`
    `s 130AE(2)(b) complete and have ready for delivery all the appropriate certificates in connection with the transfer on a notice of transfer of shares`
    `s 130AE(2)(c) complete and have ready for delivery all the appropriate certificates and debentures in connection with the transfer of debentures`

-- s 130AE(1), allotment limb: within 60 days after the allotment of any of its shares or debentures (the day of the allotment is not counted: sg-periods P1).
-- src:10981 | 130AE.—(1) Every public company must within 60 days after the
-- src:10982 | allotment of any of its shares or debentures, and within 30 days after
-- src:10983 | the date on which a transfer (other than such a transfer as the company
-- src:10984 | is for any reason entitled to refuse to register and does not register) of
-- src:10985 | any of its shares or debentures is lodged with the company, complete
-- src:10986 | and have ready for delivery all the appropriate certificates and
-- src:10987 | debentures in connection with the allotment or transfer.
@ref s 130AE(1) (src:10981-10987)
GIVEN `the day of the allotment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 130AE(1) the last day for completing the certificates after an allotment` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the allotment` 60 Days

@ref s 130AE(1) (src:10981-10987)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the allotment` IS A DATE
      `the day the certificates and debentures were complete and ready for delivery` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AE(1) the public company completed the certificates in time after the allotment` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a public company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every public company must" -- a scope limit with no "only"; the private company's rule is subsection (2)
    ELSE IF `the day the certificates and debentures were complete and ready for delivery` AT MOST (`s 130AE(1) the last day for completing the certificates after an allotment` `the day of the allotment`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must within 60 days after the allotment of any of its shares or debentures ... complete and have ready for delivery all the appropriate certificates and debentures" -- a period the text fixes in its own words

-- s 130AE(1), transfer limb: within 30 days after the date on which a transfer is lodged with the company, other than a transfer the company is for any reason entitled to refuse to register and does not register.
-- "(other than X)": a transfer the company is entitled to refuse and does not register is outside the duty, in the text's own words (fork F-j130AE-1, the "(other than X)" question of the ruling of 2026-11-05T10:25Z).
@ref s 130AE(1) (src:10981-10987)
GIVEN `the day the transfer was lodged with the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 130AE(1) the last day for completing the certificates after a transfer was lodged` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the transfer was lodged with the company` 30 Days

@ref s 130AE(1) (src:10981-10987)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a transfer of shares or debentures has been lodged with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is one the company is for any reason entitled to refuse to register and does not register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AE(1) the public company must complete the certificates after the transfer` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a public company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every public company must" -- a scope limit with no "only"; the private company's rule is subsection (2)
    ELSE IF NOT `a transfer of shares or debentures has been lodged with the company`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within 30 days after the date on which a transfer ... is lodged with the company" -- a duty that starts with a lodging; where nothing was lodged the text does not speak (a scope limit with no "only", item (c) of the periods ruling)
         ELSE IF `the transfer is one the company is for any reason entitled to refuse to register and does not register`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(other than such a transfer as the company is for any reason entitled to refuse to register and does not register)"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 130AE(1) (src:10981-10987)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the transfer was lodged with the company` IS A DATE
      `the day the certificates and debentures were complete and ready for delivery` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AE(1) the public company completed the certificates in time after the transfer` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a public company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every public company must" -- a scope limit with no "only"; the private company's rule is subsection (2)
    ELSE IF `the day the certificates and debentures were complete and ready for delivery` AT MOST (`s 130AE(1) the last day for completing the certificates after a transfer was lodged` `the day the transfer was lodged with the company`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ... within 30 days after the date on which a transfer ... is lodged with the company, complete and have ready for delivery all the appropriate certificates and debentures" -- a period the text fixes in its own words

@ref s 130AE(1) (src:10981-10987)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 130AE act`
`s 130AE(1) a public company must complete the certificates within 60 days after an allotment` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 130AE(1) complete and have ready for delivery all the appropriate certificates and debentures in connection with the allotment`
    WITHIN 60
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company did not complete and have ready for delivery the appropriate certificates and debentures within 60 days after the allotment"

@ref s 130AE(1) (src:10981-10987)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 130AE act`
`s 130AE(1) a public company must complete the certificates within 30 days after a transfer is lodged` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 130AE(1) complete and have ready for delivery all the appropriate certificates and debentures in connection with the transfer`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the public company did not complete and have ready for delivery the appropriate certificates and debentures within 30 days after the date on which the transfer was lodged"

