-- s 130AE(2)(b): a private company, within 30 days after the date on which a notice of transfer of shares is lodged with the Registrar under section 126(2) or 128(1)(a).
-- src:10999 | (b) within 30 days after the date on which a notice of transfer
-- src:11000 | of shares is lodged with the Registrar under section 126(2)
-- src:11001 | or 128(1)(a); and
@ref s 130AE(2)(b) (src:10999-11001)
GIVEN `the day the notice of transfer of shares was lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 130AE(2)(b) the last day for completing the certificates after a notice of transfer of shares was lodged` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the notice of transfer of shares was lodged with the Registrar` 30 Days

@ref s 130AE(2)(b) (src:10999-11001)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice of transfer of shares was lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
      `the day the certificates and debentures were complete and ready for delivery` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AE(2)(b) the private company completed the certificates in time after the notice of transfer of shares was lodged` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a private company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every private company must" -- a scope limit with no "only"; the public company's rule is subsection (1)
    ELSE IF `the day the certificates and debentures were complete and ready for delivery` AT MOST (`s 130AE(2)(b) the last day for completing the certificates after a notice of transfer of shares was lodged` `the day the notice of transfer of shares was lodged with the Registrar`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must (b) within 30 days after the date on which a notice of transfer of shares is lodged with the Registrar under section 126(2) or 128(1)(a) ... complete and have ready for delivery all the appropriate certificates" -- a period the text fixes in its own words

@ref s 130AE(2)(b) (src:10999-11001)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 130AE act`
`s 130AE(2)(b) a private company must complete the certificates within 30 days after a notice of transfer of shares is lodged` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 130AE(2)(b) complete and have ready for delivery all the appropriate certificates in connection with the transfer on a notice of transfer of shares`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company did not complete and have ready for delivery the appropriate certificates within 30 days after the date on which the notice of transfer of shares was lodged with the Registrar"

-- s 130AE(2)(c): a private company, within 30 days after the date on which a transfer of debentures (other than one the company is entitled to refuse and does not register) is lodged with the company.
-- src:11003 | (c) within 30 days after the date on which a transfer (other than
-- src:11004 | such a transfer as the company is for any reason entitled to
-- src:11005 | refuse to register and does not register) of any of its
-- src:11006 | debentures is lodged with the company,
@ref s 130AE(2)(c) (src:11003-11006)
GIVEN `the day the transfer of debentures was lodged with the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 130AE(2)(c) the last day for completing the certificates after a transfer of debentures was lodged` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the transfer of debentures was lodged with the company` 30 Days

@ref s 130AE(2)(c) (src:11003-11006)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a transfer of debentures has been lodged with the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is one the company is for any reason entitled to refuse to register and does not register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AE(2)(c) the private company must complete the certificates after the transfer of debentures` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a private company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every private company must" -- a scope limit with no "only"; the public company's rule is subsection (1)
    ELSE IF NOT `a transfer of debentures has been lodged with the company`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within 30 days after the date on which a transfer ... of any of its debentures is lodged with the company" -- a duty that starts with a lodging; where nothing was lodged the text does not speak (a scope limit with no "only", item (c) of the periods ruling)
         ELSE IF `the transfer is one the company is for any reason entitled to refuse to register and does not register`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(other than such a transfer as the company is for any reason entitled to refuse to register and does not register)"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 130AE(2)(c) (src:11003-11006)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the transfer of debentures was lodged with the company` IS A DATE
      `the day the certificates and debentures were complete and ready for delivery` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AE(2)(c) the private company completed the certificates in time after the transfer of debentures` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a private company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every private company must" -- a scope limit with no "only"; the public company's rule is subsection (1)
    ELSE IF `the day the certificates and debentures were complete and ready for delivery` AT MOST (`s 130AE(2)(c) the last day for completing the certificates after a transfer of debentures was lodged` `the day the transfer of debentures was lodged with the company`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must (c) within 30 days after the date on which a transfer ... of any of its debentures is lodged with the company ... complete and have ready for delivery all the appropriate certificates and debentures" -- a period the text fixes in its own words

@ref s 130AE(2)(c) (src:11003-11006)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 130AE act`
`s 130AE(2)(c) a private company must complete the certificates within 30 days after a transfer of debentures is lodged` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 130AE(2)(c) complete and have ready for delivery all the appropriate certificates and debentures in connection with the transfer of debentures`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company did not complete and have ready for delivery the appropriate certificates and debentures within 30 days after the date on which the transfer of debentures was lodged"

-- s 130AE(3): the offence of default.
-- src:11013 | (3) If default is made in complying with this section, the company
-- src:11014 | and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty
-- src:11015 | of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:11016 | exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 130AE(3) (src:11013-11016)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 130AE` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AE(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 130AE` AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section, the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet (split site (i), fork line F-j130AE-2)

@ref s 130AE(3) (src:11013-11016)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 130AE` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 130AE(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 130AE(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 130AE` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    --                          fine, months, both, default penalty
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- s 130AE(4): if a company served with a notice to make good a default fails to do so within 10 days after the service, the Court may on the application of the person entitled make an order.
-- src:11020 | (4) If any company on which a notice has been served requiring the
-- src:11021 | company to make good any default in complying with this section
-- src:11022 | fails to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the
-- src:11023 | notice, the Court may, on the application of the person entitled to have
-- src:11024 | the certificates or the debentures delivered to the person, make an
-- src:11025 | order directing the company and any officer of the company to make
-- src:11026 | good the default within such time as is specified in the order, and the
-- src:11027 | order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application
-- src:11028 | must be borne by the company or by any officer of the company in
-- src:11029 | default in such proportions as the Court thinks fit.
@ref s 130AE(4) (src:11020-11029)
GIVEN `the day the notice was served on the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 130AE(4) the last day for the company to make good the default` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the notice was served on the company` 10 Days

@ref s 130AE(4) (src:11020-11029)
GIVEN `the day the notice was served on the company` IS A DATE
      `the company has made good the default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company made good the default` IS A DATE
      `the day of the application to the Court` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 130AE(4) the company failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice` MEANS
    IF `the company has made good the default`
    THEN NOT (`the day the company made good the default` AT MOST (`s 130AE(4) the last day for the company to make good the default` `the day the notice was served on the company`))
    ELSE NOT (`the day of the application to the Court` AT MOST (`s 130AE(4) the last day for the company to make good the default` `the day the notice was served on the company`))

-- A grant gated by "if" and by "on the application": NOTHING where either gate is unmet (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-j130AE-3, as F-j91-2).
@ref s 130AE(4) (src:11020-11029)
GIVEN `a notice requiring the company to make good a default in complying with section 130AE has been served on the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AE(4) the Court may make an order directing the company and any officer of the company to make good the default` MEANS
    IF `a notice requiring the company to make good a default in complying with section 130AE has been served on the company`
       AND `the company failed to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice`
       AND `the application is made by the person entitled to have the certificates or the debentures delivered to the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If any company on which a notice has been served ... fails to make good the default within 10 days after the service of the notice, the Court may, on the application of the person entitled" -- a grant whose "if" and "on the application" gates are unmet

@ref s 130AE(4) (src:11020-11029)
GIVEN `the order is made under section 130AE(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 130AE(4) the order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application be borne by the company or by any officer of the company in default in such proportions as the Court thinks fit` MEANS
    IF `the order is made under section 130AE(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the order may provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the company or by any officer of the company in default" -- a grant limited to the order the subsection describes

